   I like this idea; it's a good bad pun. I don't think it needs to be 
restricted to confused players, since (as you say) !oGA has a pretty good
primary purpose already, but maybe there's an abuse I haven't thought of.

   Dipping in !oGA shouldn't give extra powers to armor, weapons, or tools;
but blank books, scrolls, and wands are items that explicitly /lack/ 
"abilities", so it makes sense to have them "gain ability" this way.

